/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  vlle04_two_liquids_decanter  --  a `phaseSet VLLE` flash whose three-phase
  search finds NO vapour and falls back to TWO LIQUIDS.

  A STRUCTURAL WITNESS, NOT A VALIDATED LLE.  Read this before reading any
  number it prints.

  WHAT IT PINS.  A VLLE flash always emits three ports (vapour, liquid
  alpha, liquid beta); when the Gibbs minimisation finds the vapour fraction
  below 1 %, the solver demotes the answer to a liquid-liquid split.  Until
  2026-10-05 the unit decided WHICH two-phase fallback it had by searching
  the regime's human-readable string for "VL" -- and the LL fallback's own
  string reads "two-phase liquid (LL, VLLE attempt found V beta ~ 0)", whose
  "VLLE" contains "VL".  So the beta LIQUID left on the VAPOUR port with
  vf = 1, the second liquid port carried zero, and the energy report booked
  a latent heat that never happened (498.03 kW on this very drum).  The
  decision now reads a typed field of the flash solution (`liquidLiquid`),
  and this case is the witness that it does:

      * the `vapour` port carries ZERO flow;
      * `liquidAlpha` and `liquidBeta` both carry flow, both as liquids;
      * the unit speaks the LL vocabulary (betaFraction, no V_over_F, no
        K-values, no duty -- an LL split's liquid enthalpies carry no
        excess-of-mixing term, the same posture as a `phaseSet LL` flash);
      * the plant first law closes (no phantom latent heat).

  Gate: bin/curate/check_vlle_fallback.py.  Record: DEV.md section 5, the
  entry dated 2026-10-05.

  WHY THESE NUMBERS ARE NOT PHYSICS.  The NRTL pair is Choupo's OWN
  regression to measured BUBBLE TEMPERATURES of ethanol + cyclohexane (the
  case tutorials/props/curation/curate12_nrtl_ethanol_cyclohexane, whose
  record is copied UNCHANGED into constant/parameters/NRTL/ here).  It
  passed its held-out bubble-temperature test and was deliberately NOT
  promoted to the catalogue, because it predicts a liquid-liquid split up to
  about 358.8 K while the measurements it was fitted to show ONE liquid.
  That spurious split is exactly what this witness needs -- a VLLE flash
  that ends with two liquids and no vapour -- and exactly why no composition
  it prints may be quoted as the behaviour of real ethanol + cyclohexane.
  The run's own T-x-y diagnostic at 3 bar boils every composition at or
  above about 370 K, thirty kelvin above the drum, so the ABSENCE of vapour
  is the model's honest answer at these conditions; the SECOND LIQUID is
  what its own evidence does not support.

  The copied record names `fittedInCase`, so check_regressed_pairs re-runs
  curate12 and holds this copy to the fit: it cannot drift.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        decanter01;
        type        isothermalFlash;
        model       gibbsMinimisation;      // the machine, NAMED (type -> model -> operation)
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( vapour  liquidAlpha  liquidBeta );

        operation
        {
            T          340.0 K;
            P          3.0 bar;
            phaseSet   VLLE;
            alphaRich  cyclohexane;
            betaRich   ethanol;
        }

        compositionTol   1e-5;
        maxOuterIter     200;
    }
);
